<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::supply_chain_strain" target="ai_governance_and_race::security_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stress in component and software supply chains leads firms to integrate alternative or unvetted vendors and hurried patches, increasing exploitable vulnerabilities and thus security incidents involving AI systems.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_governance_and_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::supply_chain_strain" target="global_energy_supply_sho::refining_throughput" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Wartime logistics bottlenecks and parts shortages delay maintenance and constrain delivery of critical catalysts and spares, forcing refineries to cut runs and lowering overall crude-to-fuel processing rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::supply_chain_strain" target="persian_gulf_conflict::trade_flow_loss_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened logistics and spare-parts bottlenecks (for tankers, repair yards, and port services) increase vessel downtime and rerouting costs, causing a measurable rise in losses and declines in bilateral and transit trade flows through the Persian Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">persian_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
