  <data key="d34">-</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::defense_production_rate" target="ai_governance_and_race::model_capability_growth" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased defense procurement channels funding and prioritizing AI R&amp;D and bespoke model development for military suppliers, accelerating the technical capability growth of deployed models.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_governance_and_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::defense_production_rate" target="persian_gulf_conflict::escalation_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">An accelerated flow of arms and munitions into international markets driven by increased defense production shortens procurement cycles for regional actors and enables higher-tempo operations and show-of-force deployments that raise operational escalation in the Persian Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">persian_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::defense_production_rate" target="us_china_strategic_rival::tech_competition" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in Western and allied defense procurement to arm Ukraine increases immediate global demand for advanced subsystems (avionics, sensors, microelectronics), intensifying US–China competition over suppliers, export controls and market access as both sides jockey to secure/deny those inputs.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
</edge>
