<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::strategic_autonomy_push" target="ai_governance_and_race::safety_testing_rigor" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Policies to onshore critical AI capabilities and certify domestic supply chains prompt regulators and firms to require additional in-country safety validation, independent audits and compliance testing, increasing pre-release testing depth.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_governance_and_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::strategic_autonomy_push" target="global_energy_supply_sho::diesel_trade_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Policies aimed at strategic autonomy (export controls, export taxes, import substitution mandates and accelerated stockpiling) reduce willingness to export refined products and increase domestic retention, lowering international diesel trade volumes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::strategic_autonomy_push" target="russia_ukraine_war::supply_chain_strain" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A stronger push for strategic autonomy (localization, export controls and procurement preferences) diverts components into domestic channels and erects new regulatory frictions, producing immediate bottlenecks and increased logistic/parts stress for suppliers serving the Ukraine theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
