  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Disruptions or reorientations in international diesel trade force the US and China to open emergency negotiations, supply agreements, or multilateral talks with suppliers and transit states to secure fuel lines, increasing high‑level diplomatic activity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
