<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::diesel_price_level" target="ai_governance_and_race::model_release_cadence" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp rises in diesel prices raise operational and transport costs for smaller cloud providers and on‑premise labs that rely on diesel for backup power and logistics, causing them to cut runtime and delay training/deployment schedules and thereby slow model release cadence.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_governance_and_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::diesel_price_level" target="persian_gulf_conflict::risk_premia_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in global diesel prices push up freight and fuel cost forecasts and insurer loss-exposure estimates, causing insurers and financial markets to raise conflict- and transit-related risk premia for Persian Gulf operations.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">persian_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::diesel_price_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforcement" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained global rises in diesel prices raise domestic economic and political pressure on sanctioning governments to prioritize fuel availability, leading some authorities to relax enforcement rigor or grant exemptions that reduce overall sanctions enforcement pressure.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_sho::diesel_price_level" target="us_china_strategic_rival::semiconductor_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in diesel prices increases transport and onsite energy costs for fabs and component suppliers, making cross‑border shipping and rapid redeployment of semiconductor production more costly and reducing effective capacity flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_sho</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
</edge>
